A||||2||2FASTOM||My Temp gage help please!||||1||
Z||000000||2FASTOM||08-31-2001||09:23 AM||||My fiero's temp indicator on the dash reads like 380 off the scale I replaced the Coolant temp sending unit and it's still acting up, can anyone help? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||08-31-2001||09:38 AM||||Does it read that high all the time?  Mine started doing that after I had the gauge cluster out for repairs.  Easy test:  take off the top of the guage cluster and make sure that the two bottom right and left side harnessess are pluged in all the way.  That was what fixed mine.  Apparently I didn't get a good connection when I pluged them back in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Dreamer||08-31-2001||03:01 PM||||I think what you're referring to is the defect in a good number of backlit Fiero dashes.  If it pegged when you started it a while back, chances are if you give it a good firm slap on the top of the cluster (on the vinyl) it'll free up and read actual temp.  Mine tends to peg at like 300 every now and then, and I know Rockcrawl's red GT did the same as well as others.....<P>Ryan||||reg||1
